+The remedies form their own line. After 2005 at Staniforth Road, the audible warning board was installed and a 24-metre section of fence was redesigned. After the death at Woodbourn Road in 2016, RAIB recommended that the operator review its operational standards against its training material, with the stated intent "that all tram drivers drive to the same set of requirements, irrespective of when they were initially trained." RAIB now records that more effective implementation of that recommendation "could have addressed the inconsistencies in audible warnings for users of the footpath crossing which were a factor in this accident."
 
